{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Living the Dream"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The Opportunity to Win an Offer"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 16}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands specific information in written texts "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.  Understands specific information in written texts "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands specific information in written texts "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le16ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Talking Hypothetically About the Past"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " When you want to talk about situations in the past in a hypothetical context (not real or necessarily true), you can use the structures <span class=\"italic\">would have</span>, <span class=\"italic\">should have</span> and <span class=\"italic\">could have</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Could have </span> (+ past participle) means that something was possible in the past, or you had the ability to do something in the past, but you didn't do it."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">could have called</span>, but I thought it was too late.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You also use <span class=\"italic\">could have </span> to make a guess about something that happened in the past. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Where is Denise?</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">She <span class=\"strong\">could have been </span> delayed downtown  or she <span class=\"strong\">could have overslept</span>.</span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Should have</span>  (+ past participle) means something would have been a good idea, but you didn't do it. You can use it to give advice about the past when you say it to someone else, or to express regret about what you did or didn't do when you're talking about yourself."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">should have prepared more</span>. </span> (I regret not preparing.)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">She <span class=\"strong\">should have answered </span> that question differently. </span> (She didn't answer that question very well and she should have done it differently.)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use <span class=\"italic\">would have</span> ( + past participle) to talk about something you wanted to do but you didn't do. This is very similar to the third conditional, but we don't need an 'if clause'."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">would have sent </span> a thank you e-mail, but I didn't know your address.</span> <br/> (I wanted to e-mail you but I didn't know your address, so I didn't e-mail you.)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I could have come over after nine, but I thought it was too late. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I should have called earlier in the day. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I  thought she should have said this and she could have answered that. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "She should have been much more formal and she shouldn't have talked so much."}, {"type": "example", "content": "She could have just responded with, \u201cfine, thank you\u201d or she could have asked the interviewer how he was. "}, {"type": "example", "content": " Well, that should have made you feel quite confident."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " The Future"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You can use four different tenses to talk about the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you talk about a things that are not decided or when you make a decision at the moment of speaking for the future, you use the modal <span class=\"italic\">will</span>. <br> For example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">Well, they will contact me before 3:00 p.m. Friday.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you ask about intentions, you use <span class=\"italic\">be going to</span>. <br> For example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">Based on my interview, I think I'm going to get this job!</span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you talk about things that are arranged, on the agenda or booked for the future, you use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Continuous </span>tense. <br> For example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">Are you going to send a thank you e-mail?</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you talk about schedules, you use the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Present</span>. <br> For example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">We leave at 5 tonight. </span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Well, they will contact me before 3:00 p.m. Friday."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Are you going to send a thank you e-mail?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I will do that after we leave."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'm also madly researching BFP for any other information on the web."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Based on my interview, I think I'm going to get this job! "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to hit it out of the park"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to do extremely well"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I think I hit it out of the park! "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le16ob09aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you hear when someone feels confident!"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to critique"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to analyze"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I sat there and critiqued this person's interview. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le16ob09aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "right out of the gate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "from the beginning "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I think it turned the interviewer off right out of the gate."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le16ob09aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "concisely"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " in few words"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I answered all his questions clearly and concisely."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le16ob09aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "madly"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "as fast as possible; quickly "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm also madly researching BFP for any other information on the web."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le16ob09aud05"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Watch YouTube videos about bad job interviews."}, {"type": "text", "content": "With a partner, make a list of all the faults you see."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write sentences using <span class=\"italic\">could have</span>,<span class=\"italic\">would have</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">should have</span> to explain what you would have done differently."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Present your video and report what you would have hypothetically changed to the rest of the class."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I watch a mock job interview and break down the faults in it. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make sentences using <span class=\"italic\">could have</span>,<span class=\"italic\"> should have</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">would have</span> to explain what I would change."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I present my video and share my ideas with the rest of the class."}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about events and experiences related to jobs."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can discuss hypothetical situations i